project.done — vir-search

Completion date: 2026-09-15
Commit range: 69e8b5c..6ac1b16 (17 commits on main, pushed; v1.4.3
tagged verbatim at ae10c30, GitHub Release created, CI green on every
push).

What shipped (the final audit's consolidated ranked list, top-down):

- The Display/round-trip semantic holes are closed: quote_if_needed
  quotes the grammar-intercepted bare words (true/false any case,
  wildcard shapes) through shared boundary helpers, a quoted In-list
  body degrades to literal text (gate Q1: reject), nested combinators
  render parenthesized, Not(Empty) can no longer render a bare "NOT "
  that steals the next token, and a balanced empty group claims its
  closer silently. The generated-input fuzz (5000 seeded LCG cases,
  no dependencies) guards the class permanently; its first run caught
  two of the holes.
- Ymd years outside 0..=9999 degrade at parse with a warning (gate Q3),
  killing the silent 1970-fallback range inversion.
- The regex dependency is removed (gate Q2: remove; zero use sites in
  the crate's life); lock and docs synced.
- The degradation log is bounded (100 entries, 3 per message) with a
  suppressed-count summary; unknown-field degradation keeps the whole
  visible fragment.
- 1.4.3 hygiene: Debug derives on ParseResult/QueryCache,
  examples/mini_consumer.rs (the compile-checked minimal consumer),
  API.md created.
- The comment/doc truth batch, the resolve_vl perspective-span
  coordinate documentation, the README/spec/roadmap grammar and prose
  passes, and the fold-vs-FTS5 verification (empirical; claim softened
  to the verified truth) all landed.
- GitHub: tag-triggered CI, permissions block, README badge, private
  vulnerability reporting enabled and verified.
- Cascade: one consumer wave carried everything (Atrium c34639a,
  Conservatory a3aa830; both locks at 1.4.3 @ 8087e93, suites green,
  adoption lines in their patchnotes, CI green; cargo-sources.json
  regenerated). Consumer-doc drift fixed under #117 (Atrium c2562bd,
  Conservatory 256bfed), logged in both records.

Reopen conditions (work recorded, deliberately not built):

- PENDING GATES (asked 2026-09-15 in two rounds, unanswered at blitz
  close; ask once more before building): the main-protection ruleset
  (vir-gtk-class: block force-push + deletion, bypass Brandon), the
  MSRV CI job pinning 1.85.0, logo.svg add-or-declare, and the
  Cargo.toml readme/publish=false pins.
- The diagnostic-ergonomics lane (severity, suggestions, line/col);
  the perspective-span coordinate system is documented for it (spec
  2.3, Diagnostic, parse_with_resolver).
- The SQL push-down scaffold: a recorded deferral, sequenced with
  future consumer waves; per-schema fragments stay consumer-side.
- QueryCache hit-path tuning: behind first consumer adoption.
- Calibre-parity operators (count, boolean variants, key-pair values):
  speculative until a consumer asks; bare `added:7d` stays declined.
- The streaming lexer: declined unless the push-down lane makes lexing
  hot.
